From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:31:25 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0102): never contact rustdesk.com (no public server, API
 or updates)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- id@public connections bail instead of indexing the now-empty
  RENDEZVOUS_SERVERS.
- get_api_server() no longer falls back to https://admin.rustdesk.com; "" means
  no API server, which every caller already handles.
- The software update check (api.rustdesk.com, stock RustDesk downloads) is
  disabled in do_check_software_update(), which every update path goes
  through; the Auto update option is hidden.
- NAT test and the HTTP TCP proxy skip work when no server is configured
  instead of dialling ":21116".
- User-clicked links (download, release notes, EULA, public-server guide) go
  to github.com/newtro/RemoteSmith.
- New src/remotesmith.rs holds RemoteSmith-only policy.

Plan: DEF-2, AC-6, AC-40, §4 thin-fork patch 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
